    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know it's natural but it doesn't make it better. it just makes everything feel pointless. everything is just loss after loss. i look around and there's nothing left that actually feels real or worth it. what's the point of even trying to move forward when everything just ends up being a void like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's true, understanding *why* it hurts doesn't magically make the pain disappear, and the constant feeling of loss is exhausting. When everything feels like a void, the idea of \"moving forward\" seems impossibly far away, like climbing out of quicksand. Perhaps the point isn't to find a grand reason to keep going, but to find the smallest, most manageable moment of quiet comfort in the chaos. Just let yourself be in the void for a while; you don't have to force meaning onto it right now.",
